      "text": "Above 900 °C in oxidative or corrosive environments, the Si-containing CrFeCoNiX variant forms a stable, coherent protective oxide layer.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Silicon preferentially forms a continuous, amorphous, silica-rich oxide layer on the alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The silica-rich oxide adheres to the underlying alloy substrate.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mn-containing CrFeCoNiX alloys develop heterogeneous oxide scales that crack or spall under thermal stress.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al-containing CrFeCoNiX alloys develop heterogeneous oxide scales that crack or spall under thermal stress.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The identity of X governs oxide-scale formation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mn- and Al-derived oxide phases are less cohesive than the proposed silica-rich layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Silicon oxidizes rapidly under the proposed exposure conditions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting SiO2 layer is dense and adherent.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiO2 layer fills microstructural defects.",
